    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high-ceiling production today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**, who represent our strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.36) benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Tong, with a 14% boost in efficiency due to platoon alignment and strong SP skill metrics. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (79.25) projects for elite output against Lodolo, leveraging a 17% SP skill advantage and a favorable park factor to overcome the left-on-left dynamic. **Jackson Merrill** also offers significant value (75.27); his score is bolstered by a potent combination of a 14% park boost and a massive 19% SP skill advantage against Sugano, making him a prime candidate for run production in the five-hole.\n\nManaging the margins remains crucial as we navigate several thin matchups. **Miguel Vargas** (40.41) and **Wade Meckler** (40.39) occupy the bottom of our starting lineup, both barely clinging to a start due to restrictive SP skill headwinds from Williams and Anderson, respectively. **Wade Meckler** in particular faces a tough L/L platoon disadvantage, but his utility outweighs the current bench options, most of whom remain sidelined by injury\u2014specifically **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**. While we are closely monitoring the availability of depth pieces like **Heliot Ramos** and **Nasim Nunez**, the current roster composition forces us to lean on **Coby Mayo** (50.91) in the UTIL slot. Despite a slight penalty against Tong, **Coby Mayo** remains a more stable play than our other reserve options like **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, or **Curtis Mead**, providing a reliable floor while we wait for our injured core to return. We are proceeding with caution, keeping an eye on late-breaking weather patterns that could impact these projections, though no significant flags have surfaced to trigger a lineup pivot at this time.",
